&  a_{kl} 

\\  a_{il} 

&  0 

&  a_{kl} 

&  -2w_ l 

\end{matrix} \right)  \]
</div>
<p>
 is negative definite unless $n = 4$. The case $n = 4$ can happen: then the determinant<a class="footnotemark" href="#a0001156352" id="a0001156352-mark"><sup>2</sup></a> of the matrix is zero and we obtain the equation 
</p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  16 + \frac{a_{ij}^2}{w_ iw_ j}\frac{a_{kl}^2}{w_ kw_ l} + \frac{a_{jk}^2}{w_ jw_ k}\frac{a_{il}^2}{w_ iw_ l} = 4\frac{a_{ij}^2}{w_ iw_ j} + 4\frac{a_{jk}^2}{w_ jw_ k} + 4\frac{a_{kl}^2}{w_ kw_ l} + 4\frac{a_{il}^2}{w_ iw_ l} + 2\frac{a_{ij}a_{il}a_{jk}a_{kl}}{w_ iw_ jw_ kw_ l}  \]
</div>
<p>
